## Key Decisions
- **PersonalBankStmt enum casing is exact.** Channel 165481 accepts
  PersonalBankStmt12Mos / PersonalBankStmt24Mos / BusinessBankStmt12Mos /
  BusinessBankStmt24Mos. Even tiny variants (BankStmt12Mos, PersonalBankStmt12Mo
  singular, PersonalBankStatement12Mos) fail with HTTP 400. My prior probe
  missed these because I tested case variants like BankStatement12, not the
  exact Stmt+Mos abbreviation.
- **Income map now routes bank-statement / alt-doc / tax / VOE-ish scenarios
  to PersonalBankStmt12Mos** (12mo for catch-all, 24mo only when explicitly
  selected). assetDepletion / assetUtilization continue to use AssetRelated.
  voe still uses WrittenVOE (legitimate VOE program).
- **Prepay UI collapsed from two fields to one.** "Prepay Fee" with three
  options (5% / 3% / No Prepay) is the only control. Internally it syncs
  prepayPeriod (5pct→60mo, 3pct→36mo, none→0mo) so all existing pricing
  logic + display helpers continue to function.
- **Broker view no longer filters down to one program.** All prepay variants
  returned by OB are visible; the "Selected Prepay" badge highlights the
  broker's choice. Admin view was always like this.
- **Register New Loan replaces Reserve/Lock Rate** in the row Actions
  dropdown. The Reserve/Lock email pipeline still exists (handler
  handleRowReserve + activeRowAction state) but is no longer reachable
  from the broker UI. Left in place in case user wants to reinstate it.
- **Two access intents = two emails, not two checkboxes.** Implemented as
  two stacked action buttons inside the modal — both function as
  one-click "checkbox-and-submit" per the user's spec. Visually
  distinguished: "I have access" = bordered teal (primary), "I need
  access" = bordered slate (secondary).
- **All emails route through Resend** via /api/send-email. FROM address
  must end in a verified domain (tqltpo.com or tqlend.com); our default
  TQLQuote@tqltpo.com passes the verification check.

